module fluorescence

manifest leaf_tissue
manifest trichloroacetic_acid
manifest potassium_iodide
manifest potassium_phosphate_buffer

instructions:

// Step 1: Crush leaf tissue (control or infected) with liquid nitrogen, then combine with the
// reaction mixture: TCA, KI, and potassium phosphate buffer (10 mM, pH 6.5)
tissue = dispense 100 units of leaf_tissue
tca = dispense 250 units of trichloroacetic_acid
ki = dispense 500 units of potassium_iodide
kpb = dispense 250 units of potassium_phosphate_buffer

mix1 = mix tissue with tca
mix2 = mix mix1 with ki
reaction = mix mix2 with kpb

// Step 2: Vortex/homogenize for 10 min at 4 C
heat reaction at 4c for 10m

// Step 3: Centrifugation (12,000 x g, 15 min, 4 C) is off-chip; supernatant is carried forward
// and incubated at ~25 C for 20 min before reading
heat reaction at 25c for 20m

// Step 4: Measure absorbance at 390 nm to quantify H2O2 content
// (detect fluorescence used as the generic optical-signal readout stand-in, since BioScript
// exposes no dedicated absorbance/spectrophotometric detect module)
h2o2_reading = detect fluorescence on reaction for 30s

dispose reaction
